./runs/codex_boundary_round4_review.log:3538:**C1 [MAJOR]** [Guide §5.5.2](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:393) says success requires a CI that excludes zero, which also admits a significantly *negative* increment. Its termination rule treats failure to detect a `0.25 sd` effect as futility; `MDD₈₀` does not establish equivalence. **Fix:** require a positive CI lower bound for success and an upper confidence bound below the effect floor for futility.
./runs/codex_boundary_round4_review.log:3560:**E2 [MAJOR]** [Guide §5.5.4](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:401) defines “precise zero” by CI half-width alone. A narrow CI centered on a meaningful effect would satisfy that condition; the [grid script also treats a reference winner as precise without checking alternatives](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_meta_config_grid.py:305). **Fix:** use equivalence bounds on every relevant contrast, including alternatives to the reference.
