### A. Round-5 dispositions

| Disposition | Status | Verification |
|---|---|---|
| Grid decision rule and serialized primary null | **ADDRESSED** | Script, report, and both JSON artifacts agree; saved statistics are unchanged. |
| `read_jsonl` default | **ADDRESSED** | Default is `version_policy="warn"`. |
| Persistent pooling audit | **PARTIAL** | Opt-ins append to JSONL when writable, but an append failure is silently ignored. |
| Cross-file pooling rule | **PARTIAL** | The helper checks the combined stamps; it cannot verify that each source used the same note. |
| Eight loader migrations | **PARTIAL** | Four retain calls to the removed `iter_jsonl` import; other training consumers still use raw access. |
| §2.4 parser and raw-unit report wording | **ADDRESSED** | The parser fits the live contiguous table; the report assigns fixed `sd_ref` only to the superseded result. |

### B. Issues

- **BLOCKER** — [calibration](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_rlcd_calibration_ablation.py:144), [LOO confirmatory](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_rlcd_loo_confirmatory.py:90), [LOO transfer](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_rlcd_loo_transfer.py:123), and [router panel](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_rlcd_router_panel.py:76) call undefined `iter_jsonl`. **Fix:** replace each call with `read_jsonl(..., version_policy="warn")`.
- **MAJOR** — [assert_combinable](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/dataset/versioning.py:140) turns any nonempty note into `pool_legacy=True` and cannot compare it with per-source opt-in notes. **Fix:** pass validated source decisions and require their notes to match before permitting the combined pool.
- **MAJOR** — [audit append](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/dataset/versioning.py:130) silently fails on `OSError`, so an accepted opt-in may leave no durable trail. **Fix:** fail the opt-in when the required audit entry cannot be written.
- **MAJOR** — [RLCD sweep](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/sweep_rlcd.py:37) still trains through unchecked `iter_jsonl`; [cross-family transfer](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_rq2_1_cross_family_transfer.py:319) also builds a pooled dataset that way. **Fix:** migrate remaining pooling consumers to the checked loader.
- **MAJOR** — The [screen report](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_META_CONFIG_SCREEN.md:84) and [screen script](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_meta_config_screen.py:204) still call CI half-width alone a “precise null,” conflicting with the guide’s equivalence rule. **Fix:** retain the historical rule as recorded, explicitly mark it superseded, and state the valid equivalence criterion.

### C. Standing-spec judgment

The grid result and its declared rule now align, but broken migrated scripts and unenforced pooling paths prevent the package from serving as the standing modification specification. This was a read-only review; I ran no tests or training.

VERDICT: REVISE
